ADS-004 — Canonical Engineering Artifact (CEA)

Document ID: ADS-004
Title: Canonical Engineering Artifact (CEA)
Version: 1.0.0-draft
Status: Draft

1. Purpose

This specification defines the Canonical Engineering Artifact (CEA), the normative representation of engineering cognition within the Atlas Engineering Cognition Framework (AECF).

Every engineering artifact produced, consumed, transformed, or communicated by Atlas SHALL be represented as a Canonical Engineering Artifact or one of its specializations.

2. Scope

This specification defines:

Engineering artifact model
Artifact hierarchy
Artifact lifecycle
Mandatory properties
Engineering semantics
Provenance
Cognitive relationships
Quality requirements

This specification applies to all engineering cognition within Atlas.

3. Canonical Definition

A Canonical Engineering Artifact (CEA) is a specialization of the Canonical Atlas Object that represents an engineering fact, observation, understanding, knowledge, conclusion, or recommendation within the engineering cognition lifecycle.

4. Objectives

The CEA SHALL:

Represent engineering cognition.
Preserve engineering meaning.
Preserve provenance.
Support traceability.
Support explainability.
Support reasoning.
Support decision making.
5. Inheritance

The Canonical Engineering Artifact SHALL inherit every mandatory property defined by the Canonical Atlas Object (CAO).

In addition, the CEA introduces engineering-specific semantics.

