6. Canonical Artifact Types

Atlas defines seven canonical engineering artifact types.

Artifact	Purpose
Observation	Captured engineering reality
Evidence	Validated engineering facts
Understanding	Engineering interpretation
Memory	Persisted engineering understanding
Knowledge	Generalized engineering understanding
Conclusion	Result of engineering reasoning
Recommendation	Actionable engineering guidance

Future artifact types SHALL extend this hierarchy.

7. Engineering Properties

Every CEA SHALL define the following engineering properties.

Property	Description
Artifact ID	Unique identifier
Artifact Type	Canonical artifact classification
Engineering Domain	Structural, Architectural, Civil, etc.
Engineering Context	Applicable engineering context
Engineering Intent	Engineering objective
Engineering Constraints	Applicable constraints
Confidence	Confidence assessment
Assumptions	Explicit assumptions
Evidence References	Supporting evidence
Reasoning References	Supporting reasoning
Decision References	Related decisions

These properties supplement the inherited CAO properties.

