9. Artifact Lifecycle

Every CEA SHALL progress through the following lifecycle.

Created
    │
Observed
    │
Validated
    │
Interpreted
    │
Reasoned
    │
Approved
    │
Active
    │
Archived

Lifecycle state SHALL remain independent of workflow execution state.

10. Provenance

Every CEA SHALL preserve:

Source observations
Input artifacts
Processing history
Cognitive operators applied
Producing engine
Producing workflow
Producing decision

Provenance SHALL be immutable.

11. Explainability

Every CEA SHALL maintain links to:

Supporting evidence
Engineering assumptions
Applied constraints
Reasoning chain
Confidence assessment
Alternative interpretations (where applicable)

Explainability SHALL be machine-readable.

12. Quality Requirements

Every CEA SHALL satisfy:

Engineering correctness
Completeness
Consistency
Traceability
Explainability
Confidence
Constraint compliance
Provenance integrity

Quality assessments SHALL be associated with the artifact.

13. Conformance

A Canonical Engineering Artifact conforms if it:

Inherits the CAO contract.
Implements engineering properties.
Preserves provenance.
Maintains cognitive relationships.
Supports lifecycle management.
Provides explainability references.
14. Future Evolution

Future revisions MAY introduce:

Domain-specific artifact profiles.
Simulation artifacts.
Digital Twin artifacts.
Regulatory artifacts.
AI-generated engineering artifacts.

Extensions SHALL preserve canonical engineering semantics.

